73
00:04:20.133 --> 00:04:21.877
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:22.717 --> 00:04:26.411
Grammar focus: Cleft sentences (what matters is).

75
00:04:26.711 --> 00:04:27.979
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:28.683 --> 00:04:31.600
What matters most is how you manage your emotions.

77
00:04:32.517 --> 00:04:34.087
What I need is a short break.

78
00:04:34.983 --> 00:04:37.320
What helps me is talking to a friend.

79
00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:45.226
A cleft sentence puts the important idea at the end to give it focus. The 'what' clause takes a singular verb: is.

80
00:04:45.983 --> 00:04:49.901
Be careful! Don't say: What matter most is how you feel.

81
00:04:51.867 --> 00:04:54.911
Say: What matters most is how you feel.

82
00:04:55.211 --> 00:04:57.768
'What' takes a singular verb: matters.

83
